  {
    "op": "replace",
    "path": "/contentPages/0",
    "raw": "Few things are 'sacred' to the Kirhos in the traditional sense, save for information. The most valuable thing to any Kirhos is any data that belonged to their people in ages long past. These are exceptionally rare, occasionally found on discs and hard-drives scattered throughout space.",
    "value": "在传统意义上，除信息外，鼠族几乎不将任何事物视为“神圣”。对每位鼠族人而言，最珍贵的莫过于属于他们远古先祖的任何数据。这些数据极为罕见，偶有发现于散落太空的光盘与硬盘之中。"
  },
  {
    "op": "replace",
    "path": "/contentPages/1",
    "raw": "A single data-disc is worth a fortune to a Kirhos, and anyone with information leading to their large collections of data (known as Storage Bays, Data-Centers or Omega Servers depending on who you ask) will be compensated with wealth beyond imagining...provided the Kirhos in question is wealthy enough to accomplish this.",
    "value": "一张数据光盘对鼠族人便意味着一笔财富。任何人若能提供线索，助其找到大规模数据集合（依人称不同，或称作“存储器海湾”、“数据中心”或“欧米茄服务器”），都将获得难以想象的财富回报 - 只要涉及的鼠族人足够富有，足以兑现这一承诺。"
  }
